  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "y  = b0*x + s0",
        "s0 = b1*x - a1*y + s1, and s1 = b2*x - a2*y",
        "That is the transposed direct form II, five multiplications a sample"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "The output y is fed back into the state, and that feedback buys the sharpness",
        "The whole filter is a chain of such sections, two poles in each",
        "The design gives Butterworth, whose band that passes is as flat as it can be"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What will catch you",
      "items": [
        "A coefficient a little wrong moves a pole, and a pole outside the circle runs away",
        "Sections of two poles, rather than one long recursion, is what holds that off",
        "The filter moves different frequencies by different times, thus the shape changes"
      ]
    }
  ]
